2708	 * and honest at every rung:
2709	 *
2710	 *   1. MIGRATED CERTIFICATES. Let's Encrypt certificates are portable — they
2711	 *      stay valid on whichever machine serves them — so copying /etc/letsencrypt
2712	 *      (certs, keys, `renewal/*.conf`, `accounts/`, the ssl option snippets)
2713	 *      gives zero-gap HTTPS the instant traffic moves. Step 8d does the copy;
2714	 *      fixRenewalConfigs repoints renewal at THIS server's webroot so
2715	 *      `certbot renew` keeps working afterwards.
2716	 *
2717	 *   2. HTTP-01 per hostname. This can only succeed once the name resolves HERE,
2718	 *      so it runs for names that already point at us, and is exposed as
2719	 *      `issueMigrationCertificates()` for the DNS-cutover flow to call again
2720	 *      afterwards. Every generated vhost carries a
2721	 *      `location ^~ /.well-known/acme-challenge/` so `--webroot` validates.
