2723	 *   3. DNS-01 for wildcards, through the customer's connected Cloudflare
2724	 *      account. Multi-tenant apps serve `<tenant>.<base>` and HTTP-01 simply
2725	 *      cannot issue `*.base`. The token is passed IN by the caller (it lives on
2726	 *      the Nxeon side, not on the customer's box), written to a 0600 credentials
2727	 *      file over SFTP — never an argv token — and shredded in `finally`.
2728	 *      Note a wildcard covers exactly ONE label, so `hq.stg.example.com` needs
2729	 *      `*.stg.example.com` as well as `*.example.com`; both are requested.
2730	 *
2731	 * A certificate failure NEVER fails the migration — it becomes a named,
2732	 * copy-pasteable manual step.
2733	 */
