2259	/**
2260	 * Every ABSOLUTE executable path a unit's Exec* directives will try to run.
2261	 *
2262	 * Defensive by design, because a unit file is untrusted input from another
2263	 * machine:
2264	 *   - `ExecStart=-/path`  the `-` (ignore failure), `@` (argv[0] override),
2265	 *     `+` (full privileges), `!` / `!!` (no-setuid variants) prefixes may appear
2266	 *     in any order and combination and are stripped before the path is read;
2267	 *   - quoted paths (`ExecStart="/opt/my app/bin/run" --flag`) are unquoted;
2268	 *   - an EMPTY assignment (`ExecStart=`) is systemd's list-reset and is skipped;
2269	 *   - a bare command (`ExecStart=node server.js`) is resolved from PATH by
2270	 *     systemd itself, so it is deliberately IGNORED — we cannot check it and
2271	 *     guessing would be worse than silence;
2272	 *   - a path carrying a `%` specifier (`/usr/bin/%i`) can only be resolved by
2273	 *     systemd, so it is skipped rather than mis-reported. It also would not pass
2274	 *     PATH_RE, which is what keeps every value here shell-inert.
2275	 */
